      "writtenOn": "2022-03-03T14:59:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Colin: do you know how to get hold of the lunch target from here?",
      "revId": "7ee2574d1abd9f2c3c0362e48d97aafc4b7113b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aafbc335_5642a1cd",
        "filename": "java/dex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-03T19:34:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need all this information in the dex file?  It\u0027s going to make the dex files different for different products even if the code is the same, which will reduce the efficiency of RBE.  I\u0027m not sure what purpose it serves if we don\u0027t also have the build number, and we definitely don\u0027t want that because it would make the dex files different in every build.",
      "parentUuid": "c3cd6fdd_1c24eb9b",
      "revId": "7ee2574d1abd9f2c3c0362e48d97aafc4b7113b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d728498c_75c1e451",
        "filename": "java/dex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1241761
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-03T20:19:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "None of this is for adding. I was playing around with the info and running a forrest run to see the output on the build bots.\n\nI was attempting to locate the build id and lunch variant so that the stacktrace could identify the build server from which we could download the mapping information. But you are absolutely right that we can\u0027t in general add the build id as the dex would differ for each build.\n\nThe mapping hash (as is already in the source file marker) is likely the best stable identification. But that means we need some other information in order to map a hash to either the build, or directly to the mapping file :-(",
      "parentUuid": "aafbc335_5642a1cd",
      "revId": "7ee2574d1abd9f2c3c0362e48d97aafc4b7113b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4a29b44_6091bc34",
        "filename": "java/dex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 266,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-03T20:46:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"build ID\" is just the value in build/make/core/build_id.mk, it\u0027s probably not what you want.  \"Build number\" is probably what you want, which you can get from using `$(cat)` in your command line to get the contents of ctx.Config().BuildNumberFile(ctx).\n\nWe don\u0027t have the name of the build server build, or the value of TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT.  You can reconstruct an approximation of TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT using `ctx.Config().Debuggable()` and `ctx.Config().Eng()`, but you won\u0027t be able to handle cases where the build server build has some extra suffix.",
      "parentUuid": "d728498c_75c1e451",
      "revId": "7ee2574d1abd9f2c3c0362e48d97aafc4b7113b3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f340f7f_33ee0745",
        "filename": "java/dex.go",
